  "worked_solution": "Since the given series is in the form $\\sum a{r}^{n-1},$ it is a geometric series. Notice that the index starts from $n=0$ instead of $n=1.$\n\nTo determine the sum, we use the formula for the sum ${S}_{N}$ of a geometric series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{0}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $r=5.$ Also, note that $N=5$ since there are $5$ terms in total.\n\nThe formula for the $n$th term of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=4{(5)}^{n-1},\n$$\n\nand so the first term ${a}_{0}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =4{(5)}^{0-1} \\\\  & =4{(5)}^{-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we substitute ${a}_{0}=\\frac{4}{5},r=5$ and $N=5$ into the formula for ${S}_{N}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{7} & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{(1-{5}^{5})}{(1-5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{(1-{5}^{5})}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-3\\,124) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,124}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
